10. Resilience Scoring (Supplemental Metric)

The protocol maintains a resilience score R_i(t) for each node to weight future incentives and detect abandonment. It is defined recursively:

R_i(t) = \alpha \cdot \mathbf{1}_{\text{active}}(i,t) + \beta \cdot \text{consistency}_i(t) + \gamma \cdot \text{longevity}_i(t),
\]  

where \alpha+\beta+\gamma=1, \text{consistency}_i(t) measures the inverse variance of recent scores, and \text{longevity}_i(t) = \min(1, \#\text{epochs active}/10). This is an empirical metric, not a proven theorem.


